mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;The proposed first floor rear/side extension, by
reason of its, scale and siting and flat roof form would appear incongruous and
insufficiently subservient resulting in harm and loss to the original form of
the house, its rear projection, and its relationship with the adjoining
property. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve or enhance the
character and appearance of the John Innes Merton Park Conservation Area resulting
in less than substantial harm for which there is no public benefit identified.
The proposal is contrary to Sections 66 and 72 of the Planning (Listed
Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Chapter 16 of the NPPF, Policy HC1
of the London Plan, and Policies D12.1, D12.2, D12.3, D12.4 and D12.5 of the
Merton Local Plan 2024.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
